-- 663_yearround_solo_corridor_seed_repair.sql — year-round SOLO seeds (goofy / elegant / active single_scenarios)
-- that stage the person on a route as a mere stage get a spot in the same place (2026-10-02,
-- NIGHTLY_COMPOSITION_AUDIT_PLAN.md).
--
-- Why: composition audit of delivered nightlies: year-round solo seeds that open on a route rendered route-staged 36%
-- vs 10% without (couples 43% vs 10%). scripts/fix-holiday-corridor-seeds.js --pools goofy,elegant,active: prefilter
-- 1,432, judge flagged 437, rewrite keeps each seed's own opening form ("Person at ...", "On a ..."), action and props
-- and swaps only the route noun for a spot. Every rewrite read; ~35 edited by hand.
-- NOT applied (26, plus 5 the rewriter left unchanged): seeds where the route IS the dream (all wild_rides, the shopping-cart and office-chair races, dog
-- sled and scooter runs, the duel step into the street, the palanquin procession, chess on the highway / grill in the
-- intersection gags), a catwalk railing that was already a spot, a Parisian passage that is the place itself, and 8
-- rewrites that swapped an alley for an open courtyard / plaza while keeping heavy rain words: in the render test that
-- pairing FLOODED the scene (the cyberpunk wall seed rendered waist-deep in water 2/2, one drifting to swimwear).
-- Render test on Kevin's account before any row changed (real nightly-dreams, force_slot_input on his own nightlies of
-- the same pool, gender-matched cast, 12 seeds x 2, original vs rewrite): route-staged 16/24 -> 3/24, swaps 21/24 ->
-- 24/24 (the originals lost the person 3 times). Identity mean 0.66 vs 0.61, driven by the flooded seed (excluded) and
-- one figure standing ON a wall (reworded to "at"). The new arm sits more often (seated 2/24 -> 10/24): ~1/3 of the
-- rewrites open on a sit-able spot, on ~5% of each pool's rows.
-- Every statement is guarded (still the old text), so a re-run changes nothing.
-- ROLLBACK: swap each statement's SET and WHERE text (the tool's --rollback writes it).

